     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Sanathoi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to Shiny too (and programming, actually), so I&#39;m not 100% sure, but I think you could use <span style=\"background-color:rgb(248,248,248);color:rgb(96,96,96);font-family:&quot;Source Code Pro&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.5px;white-space:nowrap\">nearPoints()</span> to select rows of data and then get the information from whichever column you want..?</div><div><br><div><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/selecting-rows-of-data.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/selecting-rows-of-data.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388681049000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0SYMpzRO0XzuxrnTFk8FRj\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/selecting-rows-of-data.html</a><br><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/plot-interaction-selecting-points.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/plot-interaction-selecting-points.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388681049000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nVgqDDW1pXXlvU5Cs6QDW\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/plot-interaction-selecting-points.html</a><br><br>Good luck! :)<br>Suthira</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
