<font color=\"#660066\">   </font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  output$plot1 &lt;- renderPlot({</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">    test &lt;- mydata()</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">    ggplot(data = test, aes(x = Cars, y = Names, group = &#39;Company&#39;, color = &#39;Cars&#39;)) +  geom_point()</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  })</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  </font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  output$selected &lt;- renderText({</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">    paste0(&quot;Cars=&quot;, input$plot1_click$x, &quot;\\n&quot;,</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">           &quot;Owner=&quot;, input$plot1_click$y)</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  })</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">  </font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">shinyApp(ui = ui, server = server)</font></div><div><br></div></div></code></div><br><div>Here, input$plot1_click$y gives coordinate. What I have to do if I want to print the y-axis components (Names, here). </div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
